EXT. SHELLED CHURCH BELFRY - DAWN

Stone walls open to the sky. A cracked bell. Smoke on the horizon.

SERGEANT ANNELIESE VOGEL, 30s, crouches with a sniper rifle. CORPORAL DESMOND OGBU, 20s, peers through binoculars. PRIVATE TEODORA IVANOVA, 20s, hugs a radio pack. LIEUTENANT RAFFERTY CROSS, 40s, studies a map. A boy, MATTEO, 11, huddles in the corner.

ANNELIESE
Desmond, status?

DESMOND
Nothing on the east road.

TEODORA
Still no word from Command.

RAFFERTY
They'll come.

TEODORA
When?

RAFFERTY
Soon.

Static. Then a faint voice.

COMMAND (V.O.)
(over radio)
Bell Tower, this is Command. Abort. Repeat, abort. Fall back to the bridge.

Teodora stares at the handset. She passes it to Rafferty.

RAFFERTY
Command, say again.

COMMAND (V.O.)
(over radio)
The bridge. Now.

Rafferty crushes the map. Anneliese tightens her scarf. Desmond stows the binoculars. Matteo looks at all of them.

MATTEO
Are we leaving?

ANNELIESE
We're leaving.

MATTEO
Can I bring the bell?

ANNELIESE
(gently)
It's too heavy, Matteo.

MATTEO
I know. I just wanted to ask.
